From: Yeoreum Yun <yeoreum.yun@arm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] coresight: use raw locks for CTI and ETM4 atomic callbacks

Backport the CTI and ETM4 device-lock conversions from upstream:

  e3044065fc2cf148d278475d5d03465ebf01248c
    coresight-cti: change cti_drvdata spinlock's type to raw_spinlock_t
  743c5a97c64d9a2fd7feb3cf9fe3651fba0359db
    coresight-etm4x: change etmv4_drvdata spinlock type to raw_spinlock_t

CPU STARTING/DYING callbacks run with interrupts disabled and cannot acquire
PREEMPT_RT sleeping spinlocks. Convert each complete device-lock domain,
including its sysfs users and the ETM4 configuration lock alias, to raw
spinlocks. Preserve the existing plain versus irqsave locking operations:
the ETM4 sysfs paths issue synchronous IPIs while holding the device lock
and must not gain a new IRQ-disable region.

The qualified vendor 6.1.83 tree predates coresight-trace-id.c and its ID-map
lock, so the newer upstream trace-ID-map conversion is not applicable.
This patch retains hotplug, CoreSight, runtime PM and debug checks. The
independent CoreSight framework lock used by perf configuration is outside
this hotplug repair and needs separate qualification.

Qualified source: D-Robotics/x5-kernel
c642eabfd7aacc4f44f2300e69d27ef1691a47d7.

Adapted for the pinned vendor Linux 6.1.83 tree.
Original upstream authorship and review trailers (both source commits):
Reviewed-by: James Clark <james.clark@linaro.org>
Reviewed-by: Mike Leach <mike.leach@linaro.org> (CTI source commit)
Signed-off-by: Yeoreum Yun <yeoreum.yun@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Suzuki K Poulose <suzuki.poulose@arm.com>

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/e3044065fc2cf148d278475d5d03465ebf01248c and https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/743c5a97c64d9a2fd7feb3cf9fe3651fba0359db]

